# Flutter client configuration. Copy to .env and fill the two client values.
# Run the Flutter app with: flutter run --dart-define-from-file=.env
# Project dashboard -> Connect: project URL and publishable key.
# A legacy anon key is also supported by Supabase; never use service_role here.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Project-owner CLI only. scripts/pacta_admin.py reads this value directly and
# never sends it to the Flutter client.
#
# - Strictly forbidden in client release builds or any file passed to
#   --dart-define-from-file: the client build cannot protect a secret key.
# - Prefer a separate process environment variable, or keep the line commented
#   in the shared template and use a dedicated local environment/file.
# - If the local .env also contains this line, never pass that file to a
#   release build; inject the client values separately instead.
# - Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys -> secret key.
# - Legacy three-part service_role JWTs are accepted through the fallback name
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY; SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY wins when both exist.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Supabase Personal Access Token (sbp_...); create it in
# Supabase Dashboard -> Account -> Access Tokens.
#
# - Used only by local Supabase CLI operations/migrations and by the
#   scripts/issue*.py acceptance scripts, which call the Management API.
# - Strictly forbidden in client release builds or any file passed to
#   --dart-define-from-file, exactly like SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY: a client build
#   cannot protect a management token.
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
